    "scientific_verdict": "Across prime, power-of-two, odd prime-power, and composite moduli q in {4, 5, 6, 8, 9}, the modular subset-sum collision probability C(a) equals (1/q) sum_{u=0}^{q-1} prod_{j=1}^m cos^2(pi u a_j / q). Because every non-zero Boolean difference x - x' in {-1, 0, +1}^m \\ {0} contains at least one unit coordinate +-1 mod q, Pr_a[f_a(x) == f_a(x') mod q] = 1/q holds universally even for composite q, yielding E_a[C(a)] = 1/q + (1 - 1/q) 2^{-m}."
  },
  "theorems": [
    {
      "id": "T1",
      "name": "Exact Cosine-Squared Product Identity for Subset-Sum Collision Probability",
      "statement": "For any weight vector a = (a_1, ..., a_m) in Z_q^m, the modular subset-sum fiber distribution P_a(z) = 2^(-m) |{x in {0,1}^m : <a, x> == z mod q}| has collision probability C(a) = sum_z P_a(z)^2 = (1/q) * sum_(u=0)^(q-1) prod_(j=1)^m cos^2(pi * u * a_j / q)."
    },
    {
      "id": "T2",
      "name": "Universal Z_q-Surjectivity of Non-Zero Boolean Differences and Exact Mean Collision Law",
      "statement": "For every modulus q >= 2 (prime or composite) and every distinct pair x != x' in {0, 1}^m, x - x' has at least one +-1 coordinate (a unit mod q), so Pr_(a ~ Z_q^m)[f_a(x) == f_a(x') mod q] = 1/q and E_(a ~ Z_q^m)[C(a)] = 1/q + (1 - 1/q) * 2^(-m)."
    },
    {
      "id": "T3",
      "name": "Exact Single-Coordinate Cosine-Squared Character Average on Z_q",
      "statement": "For every modulus q >= 2 and frequency u in {0, ..., q-1}, (1/q) * sum_(a=0)^(q-1) cos^2(pi * u * a / q) equals 1 for u = 0 and 1/2 for all u in {1, ..., q-1}."
    }
  ],
  "title": "DCP Subset-Sum Modular Collision-Entropy Audit: Cosine-Product Parseval Formula, Universal Boolean-Difference Surjectivity, and Exact Ensemble Collision Law"
